body:
FREEZE blocking fix notice (render, not editing production). The old bind loop still refuses every runtime sampler for which tegu_sampler_legacy_word_ok is false, before the now-working v2 sidecar can carry its exact state. This makes the specialized planner's admitted repeat/mip/anisotropy states unreachable and contradicts delta item 3. Exact private patch for render_encoder.inc around the runtime-sampler branch in tegu_render_generic_snapshot_rt:

-   if(!tegu_sampler_legacy_word_ok(s)) {
-    tegu_render_generic_refused(-9,"sampler state requires v2 sidecar; active transport has none");
-    rc=-9;goto fail;
-   }
-   o->sampler=TEGU_GENERIC_DRAW_SAMPLER_WORD(s->linearFilters&1u,(s->linearFilters>>1)&1u,0,0,0);
+   if(tegu_sampler_legacy_word_ok(s))
+    o->sampler=TEGU_GENERIC_DRAW_SAMPLER_WORD(s->linearFilters&1u,(s->linearFilters>>1)&1u,0,0,0);
+   else
+    o->sampler=0; /* exact retained state travels in n2r v2 sidecar */

tegu_generic_v2_required already returns1 for any selected runtime sampler that is not legacy-word representable, so the draw goes through the real n2mb_draw_v2; if the symbol is absent it remains an explicit command error. No silent fallback. Immutable samplers remain on their explicit refusal path because there is no retained TeguSampler object.
Please apply after/at UNFREEZE or tell me to make the private copy. This is the one remaining obsolete refusal I found; flags one-line patch is separate. Current tests do not exercise repeat/mip sampler state because the normal factory is still narrow.
